<year>2002</year>;<volume>58</volume>:<fpage>289</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11805259</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b33"><label>33</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mattioli</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Baldasseroni</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Curti</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Incidence rates of in-hospital carpal tunnel syndrome in the general population and possible associations with marital status.</article-title><source>BMC Public Health</source><year>2008</year>;<volume>8</volume>:<fpage>374</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18957090</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b34"><label>34</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sala</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Mattioli</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Violante</surname><given-names>FS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>[Risk assessment of biomechanical load for the upper limbs in housework] (in Italian).</article-title><source>Med Lav</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>98</volume>:<fpage>232</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17598351</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing interests:</bold> None.</p></fn><fn fn-type="other"><p><bold>Funding:</bold> This work was conducted in the context of a broader project for the promotion of research and training activities in the field of occupational health and safety, funded by INAIL (Istituto Nazionale per l&#x02019;Assicurazione contro gli Infortuni sul Lavoro), ISPESL (Istituto Superiore Prevenzione e Sicurezza sul Lavoro), Regione Emilia-Romagna and the University of Bologna.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>